10759: # (wave 27c, D1) A caller's kick request: a new request is written ATOMICALLY (a temporary file,
10760: # then a rename that never replaces) - when a kick file is already there the caller JOINS it (takes
10761: # its id) and never overwrites it. { Id; Created ($true: this caller made the request - only it
10762: # removes the acknowledgement after reading it); Error }.
